WEBVTT

00:01.850 --> 00:05.181
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.281 --> 00:08.565
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.600 --> 00:12.121
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:12.155 --> 00:15.139
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:15.173 --> 00:18.626
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.661 --> 00:21.947
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.982 --> 00:23.498
♪ All the things that make us

00:23.532 --> 00:24.883
♪ Laugh and cry

00:24.917 --> 00:26.918
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:37.165 --> 00:39.865
<i>ANNOUNCER: Do you want an excuse
to not go home this Christmas?</i>

00:39.899 --> 00:41.784
<i>Then fly Northwest Airlines.</i>

00:41.835 --> 00:44.554
<i>At Northwest Airlines,
thousands of employees</i>

00:44.589 --> 00:47.125
<i>are dedicated to delaying
and cancelling flights</i>

00:47.159 --> 00:49.193
<i>so you won't get home
for the holidays.</i>

00:49.228 --> 00:52.146
No way I'm getting you
on your connecting flight.

00:52.181 --> 00:54.415
No way we're taking off on time.

00:54.433 --> 00:57.385
Don't worry, I'm taking
this flight back to the gate.

00:57.387 --> 01:00.104
Do you think Jeff will
make it home this year?

01:00.139 --> 01:02.541
<i>No way--
because Jeff flew Northwest.</i>

01:02.574 --> 01:03.675
Thanks, Northwest.

01:03.710 --> 01:05.193
I hate my family.

01:05.227 --> 01:07.495
Ah, that looks great.

01:07.529 --> 01:10.533
You know, I think this is gonna
be our best Christmas ever.

01:10.568 --> 01:12.068
Yeah, but don't get
your hopes up, Lois.

01:12.103 --> 01:14.487
I couldn't afford to get you
what I got you last year.

01:14.522 --> 01:15.904
I know how you
like that song,

01:15.939 --> 01:17.741
so I got you two
turtledoves.

01:17.775 --> 01:20.059
Where did you get these?

01:20.093 --> 01:22.712
I went to a scientist and had
them genetically engineered.

01:22.747 --> 01:24.246
Fly, beautiful turtledoves.

01:24.280 --> 01:26.216
Bring Christmas cheer to all.

01:26.250 --> 01:28.685
(turtlesdoves screeching,
all yelling)

01:28.719 --> 01:30.787
Everybody outside-- we'll do
the rest of Christmas outside!

01:30.821 --> 01:32.355
Go, go, go!

01:32.390 --> 01:36.627
Look, Stewie, I'm hanging the
ornament you made at preschool.

01:36.661 --> 01:37.829
Just hang it up.

01:37.864 --> 01:39.414
Why do you have to narrate
everything you do?

01:39.449 --> 01:41.465
Peter, you want to put
the star on top of the...

01:41.500 --> 01:43.602
Hang on, hang on, Lois,
I always wanted to do this.

01:43.636 --> 01:46.521
Wait a second.

01:46.555 --> 01:48.656
It's coming.

01:48.690 --> 01:50.692
There it is!

01:52.945 --> 01:54.080
Huh?

01:54.114 --> 01:55.247
Eh, it's something,

01:55.281 --> 01:57.182
but you still
got a leftover "R."

01:57.216 --> 01:58.434
This was hard.

01:58.469 --> 02:00.103
I did this for you!

02:01.338 --> 02:02.906
This one's my favorite ornament.

02:02.941 --> 02:05.540
I can only imagine what it
must have been like for them

02:05.575 --> 02:07.477
on that very first Christmas.

02:07.511 --> 02:09.062
Yeah, it was probably
very moving...

02:09.097 --> 02:10.096
and fictional.

02:10.130 --> 02:11.864
Jesus lived with us
for, like, a week.

02:11.899 --> 02:13.300
What else do you need?

02:13.334 --> 02:15.719
It's the greatest
story ever told, Meg.

02:15.753 --> 02:18.388
A story that goes back
over a hundred years.

02:18.423 --> 02:20.908
<i>Yay, Star Wars!
No, Chris.</i>

02:20.942 --> 02:24.329
It's the story of Christmas
and the Immaculate Conception.

02:24.363 --> 02:25.864
You guys were born
the dirty way.

02:25.898 --> 02:29.199
Now, gather around, everybody,
and hear the awe-inspiring tale

02:29.234 --> 02:32.320
that's caused millions
and millions of deaths.

02:32.354 --> 02:34.457
Many years ago
there was a hardworking

02:34.491 --> 02:36.258
<i>young carpenter named Joseph,</i>

02:36.293 --> 02:38.960
<i>and one day, Joseph and his
friend Robby were hanging...</i>

02:38.994 --> 02:40.913
<i>CHRIS:
Guy's name was Robby back then?</i>

02:40.964 --> 02:42.599
<i>PETER:
The Bible is fuzzy on that.</i>

02:42.633 --> 02:44.049
<i>Anyway, Joseph and Robby
were hanging out</i>

02:44.084 --> 02:45.801
<i>one day when this happened...</i>

02:45.836 --> 02:48.086
<i>So, I went to see that new
Oedipus play last week.</i>

02:48.120 --> 02:50.724
Took my mother-- talk
about an awkward ride home.

02:50.758 --> 02:52.141
Barely got a good-night kiss.

02:52.175 --> 02:54.176
Hey, Joseph,
check it out.

02:57.565 --> 03:00.133
Oh, my God,
look at that body.

03:00.168 --> 03:03.037
Can't you just imagine her
standing on people's front lawns

03:03.071 --> 03:04.638
inside a cut-in-half bathtub?

03:04.672 --> 03:07.726
You should go talk to her
and see if she can talk.

03:07.760 --> 03:10.660
Uh, hi.
I'm... I'm Joseph.

03:10.695 --> 03:12.762
Oh, hello. I'm Mary.

03:12.797 --> 03:16.401
Listen, um, I was wondering if
you'd like to go out sometime.

03:16.436 --> 03:18.337
Well, sure.
That sounds nice.

03:18.371 --> 03:20.572
You know, there's
a beautiful spot outside of town

03:20.607 --> 03:22.441
where they dump
all the foreskins.

03:22.475 --> 03:24.911
You can sit on top
and watch the sunset.

03:24.944 --> 03:26.446
Oh, great, and maybe
we could slaughter a lamb

03:26.480 --> 03:28.414
and light it on fire
so that it rains.

03:28.449 --> 03:30.350
Well, let's not
go too fast.

03:30.384 --> 03:32.251
Listen, I'll see
you later, okay?

03:32.286 --> 03:34.086
I've got to go sit in a
circle with the other women

03:34.120 --> 03:36.506
and stare off
into the fields.

03:36.540 --> 03:38.089
All right,
you got a date.

03:38.107 --> 03:40.210
Yeah, I just hope it goes
better than my last one.

03:40.244 --> 03:42.712
Wow, Joseph,
that was great.

03:42.747 --> 03:44.832
Yeah, I got to say
I'm a little disappointed.

03:44.866 --> 03:46.466
When you said I could do you
in your "mudhut,"

03:46.500 --> 03:48.268
I thought you meant
something else.

03:49.705 --> 03:51.623
<i>PETER: And so Mary and Joseph
began their courtship.</i>

03:51.657 --> 03:54.124
<i>But even after several dates,</i>

03:54.159 --> 03:56.110
<i>Joseph couldn't get
to first base.</i>

03:56.144 --> 03:57.662
<i>Not just because
Mary was a virgin,</i>

03:57.697 --> 04:00.564
<i>but because baseball would not
be invented for 1,800 years</i>

04:00.599 --> 04:02.633
<i>and nobody knew what the hell
he was talking about.</i>

04:02.667 --> 04:05.955
You know this is the same picnic
basket we drowned my sister in.

04:05.973 --> 04:07.556
It was back when they were like,
"Drown all the girls,"

04:07.590 --> 04:09.624
and then they were like,
"Don't drown all the girls,"

04:09.659 --> 04:12.929
but she was born on a
drowning week, so, you know.

04:12.963 --> 04:14.398
(sneezes)

04:14.432 --> 04:17.332
Oh, look at that--
there's hardly any blood.

04:17.366 --> 04:18.701
You're very healthy.

04:18.735 --> 04:20.753
Well, I try
to take care of myself.

04:20.787 --> 04:23.490
Joseph, this is the most
fun I've had in a while.

04:23.524 --> 04:25.025
That's good, that's good.

04:25.059 --> 04:26.793
Pull your pants down.
What?

04:26.828 --> 04:28.594
Come on, this is
our seventh date.

04:28.629 --> 04:29.930
It's completely natural.

04:29.964 --> 04:31.599
Birds do it, bees do it,

04:31.634 --> 04:33.601
dinosaurs whom we live
alongside do it.

04:33.636 --> 04:34.868
Joseph, I can't.

04:34.902 --> 04:36.303
People will talk.

04:36.337 --> 04:37.838
So, what?
They'll talk in Aramaic.

04:37.872 --> 04:39.374
Do you understand that?
I don't.

04:39.408 --> 04:42.626
Look, you're very sweet,
but I have to save myself.

04:42.660 --> 04:45.228
For who? There's only
30 people in the whole world

04:45.263 --> 04:47.131
and you're related
to half of them.

04:47.166 --> 04:49.100
I can't believe how hard
you're making me work.

04:49.134 --> 04:52.004
Well, I do have
a very good virginity coach.

04:52.038 --> 04:54.440
No, no, no.

04:54.474 --> 04:56.543
Okay, I think I got it.
How's this?

04:56.577 --> 05:00.346
(imitating):
No, no, no.

05:00.380 --> 05:04.016
No, no, no.

05:04.050 --> 05:05.484
Look, I can't explain it,

05:05.518 --> 05:07.653
but something is
telling me to wait.

05:07.687 --> 05:10.022
Something deep,
deep inside of me.

05:10.056 --> 05:11.725
Stop talking like that
or I swear to God

05:11.759 --> 05:13.461
I'm gonna Pompeii
all over this blanket.

05:13.495 --> 05:15.062
(laughing):
Oh, you're silly.

05:15.097 --> 05:17.298
Come on, let's
just watch the show.

05:17.332 --> 05:20.451
(all shouting angrily)

05:20.485 --> 05:21.852
Wow, she's really getting it.

05:21.887 --> 05:24.221
Yeah, I know that girl--
that's Donna Magdalene,

05:24.256 --> 05:27.340
and her sister's a
bigger slut than she is.

05:31.246 --> 05:34.249
You know, we Jews got it right,
working with our hands.

05:34.283 --> 05:36.918
Yeah, let those eggheads
in Rome do the brain work,

05:36.953 --> 05:38.888
we Jews will do the brawn work.

05:38.921 --> 05:41.073
Hey, Italians, put a book
down once in a while.

05:41.107 --> 05:42.525
Yeah, yeah, right.
Definitely, yeah.

05:42.559 --> 05:43.974
Put a book down.

05:44.009 --> 05:45.544
Hey, so, uh,
you've been seeing

05:45.578 --> 05:47.246
that girl Mary
for some time now.

05:47.281 --> 05:48.448
She's pretty smoking.

05:48.482 --> 05:49.898
Aw, man, she is so hot.

05:49.916 --> 05:52.484
She's gonna go down in history
as "Hot Bitch Mary."

05:52.518 --> 05:54.187
You know, I'm thinking
of popping the question.

05:54.221 --> 05:56.089
Really?
Yeah, I figure I'm 14 now,

05:56.123 --> 05:57.741
I'm not getting
any younger.

05:57.775 --> 05:59.510
Hey, look,
it's the burning bush!

05:59.544 --> 06:01.261
Hail Mary,
full of guys.

06:01.296 --> 06:03.398
Oh come all
ye face-full.

06:03.432 --> 06:05.367
Come on, guys,
that's really dirty.

06:05.401 --> 06:06.399
Hi, Joseph.

06:06.433 --> 06:07.968
Hey, Mary,
what's going on?

06:08.002 --> 06:09.570
Oh, I just thought
I'd take a break

06:09.604 --> 06:11.806
from pooping in the open
street to come see you.

06:11.841 --> 06:13.073
That's nice.

06:13.108 --> 06:15.008
Listen, can you
come by my house later?

06:15.043 --> 06:17.411
There's something important
I have to share with you.

06:17.445 --> 06:18.446
Okay, sure.

06:18.481 --> 06:19.581
I'll come by
around that part

06:19.615 --> 06:20.949
of the day when
the sun goes away

06:20.983 --> 06:22.585
and we're all terrified
it will never come back.

06:22.619 --> 06:24.704
Okay, bye.

06:24.738 --> 06:26.405
Wow, you're a
lucky man, Joseph.

06:26.440 --> 06:27.439
I know.

06:27.457 --> 06:29.158
So, what have you
got going on later?

06:29.191 --> 06:31.276
I think I might hang
out in the town square.

06:31.310 --> 06:33.578
I hear an oracle from Greece
is sending a funny message

06:33.612 --> 06:35.548
and I want to be
there when it arrives.

06:43.975 --> 06:45.992
(panting)

06:49.564 --> 06:51.898
Penis.
Ha.

06:55.904 --> 06:57.204
Hey, Mary.

06:57.238 --> 06:58.688
Oh, hi, Joseph.
Come on in.

06:58.740 --> 07:00.441
Thanks, hey, listen
I just got tickets

07:00.476 --> 07:01.627
to see Cher in Bethlehem.

07:01.661 --> 07:02.794
You want to go?

07:02.828 --> 07:05.096
I guess-- how close
are the seats?

07:05.130 --> 07:06.365
Row L-X-V-I.

07:06.399 --> 07:07.765
That sounds great.

07:07.800 --> 07:10.937
But, look, Joseph, there's
something I have to tell you.

07:10.971 --> 07:12.371
I'm pregnant.

07:12.405 --> 07:13.504
From my finger?

07:13.539 --> 07:14.973
No, you don't understand.

07:15.008 --> 07:17.609
God has blessed me
with his child.

07:17.644 --> 07:20.179
You banged Kevin God
from South Nazareth?

07:20.213 --> 07:22.882
No, no, Joseph,
I mean God.

07:22.917 --> 07:25.051
I'm carrying God's baby.

07:25.085 --> 07:27.321
He-he sent down an angel.

07:34.445 --> 07:35.412
(gasps)

07:35.447 --> 07:36.546
Fear not, pretty lady

07:36.580 --> 07:38.715
who ain't never
had no relations.

07:38.749 --> 07:41.485
I's been sent to bring you
the message that tonight

07:41.520 --> 07:44.389
you's gonna be getting
pregnant with the Son of God.

07:44.423 --> 07:46.374
It's a miracle, yay!

07:46.409 --> 07:47.575
I am?

07:47.609 --> 07:49.527
Yeah, and it's gonna
be here soon,

07:49.561 --> 07:51.129
so you might want
to spruce yourself up.

07:51.164 --> 07:53.064
Maybe walk in the
creek a little bit.

07:53.099 --> 07:55.600
Oh, and he probably don't
want me to tell you this,

07:55.635 --> 07:57.368
but be ready 'cause
he might give you

07:57.402 --> 07:59.437
a little bit of
a donkey punch.

07:59.472 --> 08:01.339
So you're saying God
got you pregnant?

08:01.374 --> 08:04.477
Yes, Joseph.
Glory in the highest!

08:04.511 --> 08:06.712
Well, if it his will,
then his will be done,

08:06.747 --> 08:08.514
and I am but his
humble servant.

08:08.549 --> 08:09.682
But I do have one question.

08:09.716 --> 08:10.884
Was he bigger than me?

08:10.919 --> 08:12.552
Joseph,
it wasn't like that.

08:12.586 --> 08:14.620
I felt nothing.

08:14.655 --> 08:16.306
Oh, little guy.

08:21.704 --> 08:24.372
<i>ANNOUNCER: We now return
to A Christmas Carol.</i>

08:24.406 --> 08:26.457
(wind blows)

08:26.492 --> 08:29.410
I am the Ghost
of Christmas Past.

08:29.444 --> 08:31.079
Oh, hello.

08:31.113 --> 08:34.134
I am here to show you
how you lost your way.

08:34.168 --> 08:35.969
Um, oh, okay.

08:36.003 --> 08:37.803
How long is this gonna take?

08:37.838 --> 08:40.389
I don't know,
maybe eight minutes?

08:40.423 --> 08:43.843
Okay, hang on, I just
got to use the bathroom.

08:45.179 --> 08:47.180
(urinating)

08:56.859 --> 08:58.877
(urinating
continues)

09:16.163 --> 09:18.164
(urinating
continues)

09:20.900 --> 09:22.902
(tapping buttons)

09:32.814 --> 09:34.815
(urinating
continues)

09:40.957 --> 09:43.658
I am the Ghost
of Christmas Pres...

09:43.693 --> 09:46.326
Wait, you haven't gone yet?
No.

09:46.360 --> 09:48.762
(urinating stops)
Okay, here we go.

09:48.797 --> 09:52.200
(farts) Sorry this is turning
into something else.

09:52.235 --> 09:54.202
All right, kids,
gather around.

09:54.237 --> 09:57.122
Time to make our yearly terrible
call to Great Aunt Helen.

09:57.156 --> 09:59.625
(buttons beep)

09:59.660 --> 10:00.792
(phone rings)

10:00.826 --> 10:02.695
HELEN:
Hello?

10:02.728 --> 10:06.433
Hi, Aunt Helen, it's Peter,
Lois and the whole family.

10:08.302 --> 10:10.303
Peter's lowest what?
We're calling to say Merry Christmas...

10:12.673 --> 10:15.142
Are you there, dear?
We-we were just calling to...

10:16.678 --> 10:18.862
We had quite a cold snap here.
I hope you got our card.

10:18.896 --> 10:20.897
Okay, nobody talk-- we'll
just wait for her to talk.

10:25.704 --> 10:27.405
Are you still there, dear?
Well, we just wanted to...

10:27.439 --> 10:29.374
Damn it!

10:29.408 --> 10:31.509
So, how was the...
It's been rather cold.

10:31.543 --> 10:34.278
The pond froze over
a family of raccoons.

10:36.714 --> 10:38.316
Are you there, dear?
All right, well, Merry Christmas.

10:38.350 --> 10:41.987
Dad, can we hear more of that
story about the baby Jesus?

10:42.022 --> 10:44.156
Ah, right. Now
everybody listen up

10:44.190 --> 10:47.026
while I stuff the rest of this
rhetoric down your throats.

10:47.060 --> 10:48.261
Now, if you remember,

10:48.279 --> 10:51.814
Mary and Joseph were on
their way to Bethlehem.

10:53.899 --> 10:55.934
Uch, look at that.

10:55.952 --> 10:57.403
I remember when this
was all desert.

10:57.437 --> 10:58.771
You know, when
the baby comes,

10:58.789 --> 11:00.490
we could probably
homeschool him.

11:00.541 --> 11:02.709
I can count up to nine.

11:02.743 --> 11:04.778
Yeah, hey, so tell me
one more time how it is

11:04.796 --> 11:06.046
that God got you pregnant.

11:06.080 --> 11:07.381
<i>'Cause when you tell me
the story,</i>

11:07.416 --> 11:08.666
it sorta makes sense.

11:08.717 --> 11:10.116
But then when I tell
the guys at work,

11:10.134 --> 11:11.802
they poke all kinds
of holes in it.

11:11.837 --> 11:14.287
So, you guys are going
to Bethlehem, huh?

11:14.305 --> 11:16.673
I went there one time on
a donkeys' night out.

11:16.724 --> 11:19.977
<i>Oh, my God,
I got so hammered!</i>

11:20.012 --> 11:23.765
(electrical whirring)

11:23.799 --> 11:27.134
<i>PETER: And as Mary and Joseph made
their way to Bethlehem,</i>

11:27.152 --> 11:30.805
<i>three wise men were preparing
for a journey of their own.</i>

11:30.823 --> 11:31.858
<i>Chris, did you get a haircut?</i>

11:31.909 --> 11:33.308
<i>CHRIS:
I did.</i>

11:33.326 --> 11:35.110
<i>PETER: I'm just noticing.
It looks nice.</i>

11:36.346 --> 11:37.846
Hey, what's this?

11:39.782 --> 11:41.883
Hey, you guys, this says
a King of Kings

11:41.918 --> 11:43.086
will be born
in Bethlehem,

11:43.120 --> 11:44.821
and we are to go
and pay tribute.

11:44.855 --> 11:46.155
Hey, let me see that.

11:46.190 --> 11:48.559
This says,
"Three Magi or Resident."

11:48.593 --> 11:50.728
I don't think th
really care if it's us.

11:50.762 --> 11:51.961
Yeah, I don't want
to go, either.

11:51.995 --> 11:54.933
Hey, isn't your mother-in-law
visiting tomorrow?

11:54.967 --> 11:56.835
We're off
to Bethlehem!

11:56.869 --> 11:59.536
(canned laughter)

11:59.571 --> 12:02.239
<i>♪ Wise men. ♪</i>

12:05.478 --> 12:08.029
Wow, I can't believe
we're ready here.

12:08.064 --> 12:10.065
Yeah, it's amazing how
small the world is now

12:10.116 --> 12:11.449
thanks to mules
and camels.

12:11.485 --> 12:12.784
You're anywhere,
just like that.

12:12.818 --> 12:14.736
Oh, my!

12:14.787 --> 12:17.572
You can really tell
we're in the big city now.

12:17.623 --> 12:18.791
Yeah, they got everything here.

12:18.825 --> 12:20.077
They got restaurants,
they got museums.

12:20.127 --> 12:21.626
They even got movies.

12:21.660 --> 12:25.080
<i>ANNOUNCER: Coming soon, get ready
to start seeing double!</i>

12:25.114 --> 12:27.716
<i>It's Ben-Him and Ben-Her!</i>

12:27.751 --> 12:30.152
<i>Starring Adam Sandler and...</i>

12:30.187 --> 12:33.156
<i>Adam Sandler?!</i>

12:33.191 --> 12:35.459
Yoo-hoo, Benny!

12:35.493 --> 12:37.761
That's my brother
on that chariot!

12:37.812 --> 12:39.480
I'm driving here!

12:39.515 --> 12:40.514
Whoa...!

12:42.016 --> 12:44.000
(groans)

12:44.035 --> 12:46.069
Ooh, that's gotta hurt!

12:46.104 --> 12:47.405
(Announcer laughing)

12:47.439 --> 12:49.474
<i>ANNOUNCER:
And introducing that joke!</i>

12:49.508 --> 12:51.509
Ben-Him and Ben-Her!

12:51.543 --> 12:53.979
<i>Even Noah wouldn't put
these two together!</i>

12:54.013 --> 12:55.948
Cover your privates!

12:55.982 --> 12:57.866
Everyone can coli-see-um!

13:01.171 --> 13:02.921
<i>PETER:
Meanwhile, the three wise men</i>

13:02.956 --> 13:05.123
<i>were making their way
across the desert.</i>

13:05.174 --> 13:06.675
Hey, did you hear
they're coming out

13:06.709 --> 13:08.243
with four more
Commandments?

13:08.261 --> 13:10.597
Uch, all that stuff does is
interfere with small business.

13:10.631 --> 13:13.348
Oh, no, we're
out of water.

13:13.383 --> 13:14.750
We gotta
stop somewhere.

13:14.768 --> 13:16.719
Look. That's
King Herod's palace.

13:16.753 --> 13:18.589
Maybe we can get
water over there.

13:18.623 --> 13:21.125
QUAGMIRE: Wow, look at that classy,
Middle Eastern house

13:21.159 --> 13:22.759
with gold and marble.

13:22.777 --> 13:24.427
People will always want
to live next

13:24.445 --> 13:27.148
to big Middle Eastern houses
with gold and marble.

13:27.182 --> 13:29.884
Uch, I'm so bored.

13:29.918 --> 13:31.017
How's the TV coming?

13:31.052 --> 13:33.354
We are a long way off.

13:33.388 --> 13:34.889
Excuse me.

13:34.923 --> 13:38.026
We are three wise men
on a long journey.

13:38.060 --> 13:39.711
Could we trouble you
for some water?

13:39.729 --> 13:42.631
Sure. Not quite wise enough
to pack any, huh?

13:42.665 --> 13:44.167
So, what brings you to Judea?

13:44.201 --> 13:46.669
We're on our way to Bethlehem
to see a magic baby.

13:46.703 --> 13:48.104
Magic baby?
What's he do,

13:48.138 --> 13:49.603
card tricks,
rabbit in the hat?

13:49.638 --> 13:50.956
Would he let someone
in the audience

13:50.990 --> 13:52.225
punch him in
the stomach?

13:52.259 --> 13:54.210
I'd like to punch a
baby in the stomach.

13:54.244 --> 13:55.443
You can't punch
this baby.

13:55.478 --> 13:56.846
He's the Messiah.

13:56.880 --> 13:58.881
Yes, they're even calling him
the King of Kings.

13:58.916 --> 14:00.784
Yuck.
He already sounds like a dick.

14:00.818 --> 14:02.201
Okay, then how about this?

14:02.236 --> 14:03.903
I'm the King of King
of Kings.

14:03.937 --> 14:05.239
Ha! New name! Called it!

14:05.273 --> 14:07.541
Sounds like somebody's
a little threatened.

14:07.575 --> 14:10.010
No, I'm not. Would a guy who
feels threatened make sure

14:10.044 --> 14:11.645
all his advisors
are shorter than him?

14:11.679 --> 14:13.197
Ha! You said
it, King!

14:13.231 --> 14:14.330
That's telling him!

14:14.364 --> 14:15.365
Big guy!

14:15.400 --> 14:17.552
You know what?
Still, just to be safe,

14:17.586 --> 14:19.354
I should probably kill
that baby.

14:19.388 --> 14:21.956
Then Jodie Foster will love me.

14:25.160 --> 14:26.561
Welcome to the
Motel Shiksa.

14:26.595 --> 14:28.531
We won't leave the
light on for you,

14:28.565 --> 14:30.765
because what, do I work
for the electric company?

14:30.799 --> 14:33.067
Yes, we were wondering
if you had a room available?

14:33.102 --> 14:35.303
Sorry, we're all booked up--
Cher's in town.

14:35.337 --> 14:37.305
You won't find a room
in the city.

14:37.339 --> 14:39.691
No room? Joseph,
what are we gonna do?

14:39.725 --> 14:41.827
Don't worry.
I got this covered.

14:41.861 --> 14:43.395
No rooms, eh?

14:43.430 --> 14:46.265
Well, perhaps you have a room
for my good friend

14:46.299 --> 14:47.933
fistful of sand.

14:47.968 --> 14:49.035
Where's your money?

14:49.070 --> 14:50.353
I spent it on sand.

14:50.388 --> 14:52.005
I'm sorry,
I can't help you.

14:52.039 --> 14:53.207
But, sir, please,

14:53.242 --> 14:55.874
my wife is with child
and about to give birth.

14:55.909 --> 14:58.428
And I am with burrito
and about to do the same.

14:58.462 --> 15:02.432
Sir, if you don't leave now,
I'm gonna have to call IX-I-I.

15:02.466 --> 15:04.434
Yeah, we, we did one
of those earlier.

15:04.468 --> 15:05.636
Yours is better, though.

15:05.671 --> 15:07.339
We probably should've waited
for yours.

15:07.373 --> 15:09.441
(groaning)

15:09.475 --> 15:10.708
Joseph, my water
just broke!

15:10.742 --> 15:11.927
It's time!

15:11.961 --> 15:13.160
Oh, my God!

15:13.195 --> 15:15.597
<i>Please, you've gotta
have some place for us!</i>

15:15.632 --> 15:16.698
We're desperate!

15:16.733 --> 15:19.100
Well, there's
a manger out back.

15:19.134 --> 15:20.935
You can stay there.

15:20.969 --> 15:22.604
That's fine, that's fine!
We'll take it!

15:22.639 --> 15:24.207
CHER (in distance):
Bethlehem!

15:24.241 --> 15:26.342
I have one question for you!

15:26.377 --> 15:27.676
(pop song plays)

15:27.710 --> 15:31.614
♪ Do you believe in life
after love? ♪

15:31.649 --> 15:34.350
Dah... See?
I told you she'd open with that.

15:40.025 --> 15:43.362
So, Joseph and Mary
were turned away from the inn.

15:43.396 --> 15:44.863
But, Dad, I still
don't understand

15:44.897 --> 15:46.364
the whole Immaculate
Conception thing.

15:46.398 --> 15:49.034
How can anyone get pregnant
without having sex?

15:49.069 --> 15:50.870
Oh, there's lots of
stories of that, Meg.

15:50.904 --> 15:52.239
Cleveland's got
a cousin who had

15:52.273 --> 15:53.573
eight girlfriends
get pregnant,

15:53.608 --> 15:56.042
and he says he's not
responsible for a single one.

15:56.077 --> 15:57.612
Good guy.
You shake his hand,

15:57.646 --> 15:59.680
it feels like you're
touching a nice briefcase.

15:59.715 --> 16:01.798
But back to our story.

16:05.336 --> 16:07.320
All right, here we are.

16:07.355 --> 16:08.723
This seems pretty gross.

16:08.757 --> 16:11.508
I can't believe my baby's
gonna be the Son of God.

16:11.542 --> 16:13.711
Looks like all those
years fighting off

16:13.745 --> 16:16.380
my own father's advances
have finally paid off.

16:16.416 --> 16:18.015
What shall we name him?

16:18.050 --> 16:19.834
Well, this is kinda
like a barn.

16:19.868 --> 16:21.303
We could call
him Barney.

16:21.337 --> 16:22.304
Yeah, maybe.

16:22.338 --> 16:23.938
Or I kinda always
liked Tristan.

16:23.972 --> 16:25.207
Oh, my God, you want him

16:25.241 --> 16:26.841
to get the crap
beat out of him?

16:26.875 --> 16:28.743
They will crucify him
with a name like that.

16:28.777 --> 16:30.646
No, no, no.

16:30.680 --> 16:32.598
What are you doing?
How long you been there?

16:32.632 --> 16:34.550
Those names is no good.

16:34.584 --> 16:36.685
Look, why don't y'all
just give me a list,

16:36.719 --> 16:39.289
I'll run 'em up to God,
and see if he picks one.

16:39.323 --> 16:41.391
No... no...

16:41.425 --> 16:43.459
That's the name
of a champagne.

16:43.494 --> 16:44.760
No... no...

16:44.794 --> 16:45.929
Terrible!

16:45.963 --> 16:47.130
These are all
just terrible!

16:47.164 --> 16:48.332
Relax, God.

16:48.366 --> 16:50.851
You want me to get y'all
some wine and cheeses?

16:50.886 --> 16:52.486
Wait, what'd you
just say?

16:52.520 --> 16:56.241
Cheeses.
You want some cheeses?

16:56.275 --> 16:57.908
And that's why you're
allowed to eat

16:57.943 --> 17:02.513
as much mozzarella as
you want in any church.

17:02.531 --> 17:05.568
<i>So the three wise men set off
again on their journey.</i>

17:05.618 --> 17:06.985
You sure this is
the right way?

17:07.019 --> 17:09.870
Yes, I'm sure.
We follow the star.

17:09.905 --> 17:11.740
Are you sure
that's a star?

17:11.791 --> 17:13.159
We've had this
conversation!

17:13.193 --> 17:14.826
Yes, it's a star!

17:14.860 --> 17:16.328
It's got flashing
red lights!

17:16.362 --> 17:18.630
<i>Oh, my God!
It is a (bleep) plane!</i>

17:18.664 --> 17:21.000
And I said that yesterday,
you stupid idiot!

17:23.186 --> 17:25.271
Hey, thanks for coming out
on such late notice, Doc.

17:25.305 --> 17:27.908
Oh, you don't have to thank me.
This is a big deal.

17:27.942 --> 17:30.494
It's not every day that God
bestows a woman with his son.

17:30.528 --> 17:32.479
Has it ever happened before?
Yeah, once.

17:32.513 --> 17:34.314
But the woman drank
during her pregnancy.

17:34.349 --> 17:36.149
The kid came out
a real lemon.

17:36.184 --> 17:38.953
I turned this
water into poo!

17:38.988 --> 17:40.388
Uh-huh.

17:40.422 --> 17:42.857
I also turned this
fish into poo!

17:42.891 --> 17:44.291
Ah...

17:44.325 --> 17:46.194
Do you want your
birthday present?

17:46.228 --> 17:48.781
I think I know
what it is.

17:48.832 --> 17:51.382
(laughs) It's a
cashmere sweater.

17:51.417 --> 17:52.582
Oh, wow!

17:52.617 --> 17:56.404
That's actually
really nice.

17:56.422 --> 17:57.406
And now it's poo!

17:57.424 --> 17:58.840
(shrieks)

18:01.411 --> 18:03.145
Well, here we are.

18:03.179 --> 18:04.413
Okay, guys,
squeeze in.

18:04.447 --> 18:06.049
Bible photographer.

18:06.083 --> 18:07.817
Okay, we're smiling,

18:07.852 --> 18:10.053
we're happy to
see Jesus.

18:10.087 --> 18:12.056
There we go.

18:12.090 --> 18:13.790
Hey, guys,
watch your step in there.

18:13.824 --> 18:16.559
That floor's gonna be dripping
in virgin olive oil.

18:16.594 --> 18:18.161
That's kinda hot.
Gross.

18:18.195 --> 18:21.648
Hello, we are
the three wise men.

18:21.682 --> 18:23.950
We came here
following a star.

18:23.985 --> 18:26.019
Those two statements
contradict each other.

18:26.053 --> 18:27.822
We also come
bearing gifts.

18:27.856 --> 18:29.174
I brought frankincense.

18:29.208 --> 18:30.224
I brought myrrh.

18:30.258 --> 18:32.059
And I brought you
a breast pump,

18:32.094 --> 18:34.228
which in these times
is just a guy.

18:34.262 --> 18:35.563
When do I start?

18:35.597 --> 18:37.632
Oh he's coming!

18:37.667 --> 18:39.685
Oh, it hurts so bad!

18:39.719 --> 18:41.403
God, I hate working
on Christmas.

18:41.437 --> 18:43.205
Oh, here he comes.

18:46.442 --> 18:49.227
And... BC turns to AD!

18:49.263 --> 18:51.029
How's everybody doing?

18:51.064 --> 18:52.615
Oh, he's a miracle!

18:52.649 --> 18:55.218
Hey, if you're a virgin, how
come I shot out of there

18:55.252 --> 18:57.352
like a greased-up
cannonball?

18:57.387 --> 18:59.388
Greetings!
I have come to see

18:59.422 --> 19:03.159
the newborn king, but sadly,
I bring no gift.

19:03.193 --> 19:04.961
Well, what do you got
in your hand there?

19:04.995 --> 19:06.463
Uh, my drum.

19:06.498 --> 19:08.165
Well, then it looks like
you got him a drum.

19:08.199 --> 19:11.318
Pretty good gift.
But this is all I own.

19:11.353 --> 19:13.487
It's what makes me
the "Little Drummer Boy."

19:13.521 --> 19:16.457
Yeah, the baby
wants the drum.

19:16.492 --> 19:18.677
Yeah! Drum!

19:18.712 --> 19:21.262
Okay, nobody touch my hair.
I'm growing it out.

19:21.297 --> 19:23.148
Also, I'm gonna start dieting
and working out

19:23.182 --> 19:24.581
so I'm like crazy lean

19:24.616 --> 19:26.518
for the, you know, for, for,
for the thing.

19:26.552 --> 19:27.720
(hoofbeats approaching)

19:27.754 --> 19:29.055
What the deuce?

19:31.158 --> 19:33.743
Bring out the Christ Child!
We want him!

19:33.777 --> 19:34.860
Uh-oh.

19:34.895 --> 19:36.362
(whirring)

19:41.534 --> 19:45.371
I may have a virgin mom,
but I am one bad mother.

19:48.992 --> 19:50.710
(horse whinnies)

19:58.437 --> 20:00.388
Ah! Ah! You guys get him!
You guys get him!

20:00.422 --> 20:01.889
I forgot something
at the palace!

20:04.342 --> 20:07.061
Pa-choo! Pa-choo!
(makes explosion sound)

20:07.096 --> 20:09.364
And that is the
story of Jesus.

20:09.399 --> 20:11.133
That was awesome, Dad!

20:11.167 --> 20:12.483
Oh, my God! I
just realized

20:12.518 --> 20:15.052
that's the same Jesus as
the Jesus from church!

20:15.088 --> 20:16.822
That's a beautiful story,
Peter,

20:16.856 --> 20:18.223
about people coming together

20:18.258 --> 20:20.359
to form something
greater than themselves.

20:20.393 --> 20:21.928
(knocking on door)

20:22.779 --> 20:23.880
Yes, can I help you?

20:23.914 --> 20:25.197
Hi. We're from out of town

20:25.231 --> 20:26.665
and our car
just broke down!

20:26.699 --> 20:28.601
My wife's in labor.
Can we use your phone?

20:28.636 --> 20:29.601
What?! No!

20:29.636 --> 20:30.869
LOIS:
Peter, who is it?

20:30.904 --> 20:32.689
Couple of freaking scumbags
working some scam,

20:32.723 --> 20:34.592
saying how they want
to use our phone.

20:34.626 --> 20:37.293
What?! Do they want all the
presents under the tree, too?!

20:37.328 --> 20:38.429
Get rid of 'em!

20:38.463 --> 20:40.531
They're not gonna
do that, are they?

20:40.565 --> 20:42.300
Dad, shut the door,
it's freezing!

20:42.335 --> 20:43.601
Please, you've
gotta help us!

20:43.635 --> 20:44.970
You're lucky
it's Christmas

20:45.004 --> 20:46.838
or I'd call the cops on
you dirty grifters!

20:46.873 --> 20:49.907
Now you and your whore
wife get out of here!

20:49.941 --> 20:53.695
Peter, you handled
that perfectly.

20:53.729 --> 20:55.530
Merry Christmas,
Lois.

20:55.565 --> 20:57.966
MAN: Please!
We're begging you!

20:58.000 --> 20:59.385
I'm getting
the baseball bat.

20:59.386 --> 22:00.486
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru